id: pm-vcs-o3jj
title: Absorb pm 2026.8.7 merge and toolchain contracts
description: "Update pm-vcs to the published pm CLI and pm-changelog 2026.8.7 toolchain, install the extension-asset merge fence, and re-prove package health from a fresh dependency install."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: compatibility,merge-safety,multi-agent,pm-cli,toolchain
created_at: "2026-08-07T12:45:56.604Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T13:01:55.697Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-07T13:01:55.680Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-07T13:01:55.680Z"
claim_principal: codex
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The lockfile resolves @unbrained/pm-cli and pm-changelog 2026.8.7 from a fresh npm install; .gitattributes contains the canonical extensions/** no-merge and .managed-extensions.json pm-json rules; pm validate and read-only strict pm health pass without merge-fence drift; complete configured tests, exact coverage, documentation, dependency, packaging, and acceptance gates pass; the historical-identity gate fails closed only for pm-vcs-mhbz; any all-source lint or duplication gap found by the audit is explicitly tracked; no release or publication occurs"
definition_of_ready: Published pm CLI and pm-changelog 2026.8.7 are verified on npm; canonical checkout is clean; package has no open pull request
value: Keeps branch-safe PM metadata protected when multiple agents merge extension-bearing workspaces
impact: Prevents generated extension assets from entering semantic item merges and removes stale toolchain behavior from CI and local acceptance
outcome: pm-vcs is reproducibly validated against the current published PM toolchain
why_now: The fleet audit found pm-vcs missing both new 2026.8.7 extension merge rules and its lockfile still resolves pm CLI 2026.8.6
parent: pm-vcs-tr2a
reviewer: maintainer
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-08-compatibility
release: Unreleased
resolution: "Advanced the development PM toolchain to 2026.8.7, installed the canonical extension-asset merge fence, and isolated disposable installed-CLI children from linked-test tracker variables."
expected_result: pm-vcs uses the published 2026.8.7 PM tooling and merge contract while all compatibility gates pass and release blockers remain fail-closed.
actual_result: "Fresh npm ci resolved pm CLI and pm-changelog 2026.8.7; 555 tests and exact configured 100/100/100 coverage passed with every functional, documentation, packaging, and tracker-health gate. The existing historical identity audit still correctly refuses publication, and the newly identified all-source lint/duplication gap is tracked as pm-vcs-op2c."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-op2c,related_to,"2026-08-07T13:01:47.157Z",codex,pm-audit,asserted
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T12:46:41.753Z",codex,"Verified npm latest for both @unbrained/pm-cli and pm-changelog is 2026.8.7. A lock-only install initially preserved pm CLI 2026.8.6 under the old range, so both devDependency ranges were advanced to ^2026.8.7 and a clean npm ci now resolves 2026.8.7 for both with zero install-audit vulnerabilities. The runtime peer compatibility floor remains >=2026.8.1."
  "2026-08-07T12:52:06.129Z",codex,"The first linked run passed health, self-host, production audit, changelog, docstring, and pack gates but failed native-TOON, stat-cache, coverage, and npm test because linked tests intentionally export sandbox PM_PATH variables. Both acceptance scripts inherited those variables into disposable child projects, so pm 2026.8.7 safely refused pm init against the discovered sandbox tracker. Child PM invocations now clear PM_PATH, PM_GLOBAL_PATH, PM_SOURCE_PM_PATH, and PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT; native TOON and Linux strace stat-cache acceptance both pass in schema-sandbox context."
  "2026-08-07T12:54:20.928Z",codex,"After the acceptance scripts were isolated, exact coverage narrowed to one remaining failure: the fresh-clone preflight test's direct pm merge install child still inherited the linked sandbox PM_PATH and installed drivers into the wrong repository. The test now clears the same four PM context variables for that child, ensuring it proves clone-local driver installation even under an agent-linked test runner."
  "2026-08-07T13:01:47.157Z","harness:codex","Final verification on 2026-08-07: npm test passed 555/555; npm run coverage reported exact 100.00 percent lines, branches, and functions across all 27 configured production source files; typecheck, build, 30-file docstring gate, native TOON, installed-CLI strace stat-cache, byte-identical self-host, production dependency audit, dry-run package, changelog check, pm validate, and strict read-only pm health passed. npm run audit:identities correctly remains red on one undisclosed non-public historical address under pm-vcs-mhbz; no publication was attempted. Validation retains only pre-existing legacy metadata/resolution warnings plus unowned LICENSE. The audit also found that the two acceptance scripts are outside the configured coverage source set and that no explicit lint or duplicate-code release gate exists, now tracked independently as pm-vcs-op2c rather than overstating the configured 100/100/100 result."
